    "summary": "Verified motion prompt by @BThreeAgency",
    "contentBody": "Using the linked Figma frame build a badge unlock screen. Match the design exactly. Use the file's assets, lighting, type and layout and add only the motion. Animate the badge so it feels premium and celebratory. Build its scene and then celebrate with gold particles. Treat the badge as a solid 3D object that tilts toward the\\ncursor following the rules of physics. Keep it fast and smooth, it should not be bouncy.",
    "originalPrompt": "Using the linked Figma frame build a badge unlock screen. Match the design exactly. Use the file's assets, lighting, type and layout and add only the motion. Animate the badge so it feels premium and celebratory. Build its scene and then celebrate with gold particles. Treat the badge as a solid 3D object that tilts toward the\\ncursor following the rules of physics. Keep it fast and smooth, it should not be bouncy.",
    "improvedPrompt": "<direction>\nBuild a badge unlock screen from {{design}}. Match the design exactly: use the file's assets, lighting, type and layout, and add only the motion.\nThe badge unlock should feel premium and celebratory: build its scene, reveal it, then celebrate with {{celebration}}.\nTreat the badge as a solid 3D object that tilts toward the cursor following real physics (mass, damping), fast and smooth, never bouncy.\nBanned: overshoot, wobble, glows the design doesn't have, anything that looks like a template.\n</direction>\n\n<structure>\nThe scene builds in, the badge arrives and settles with weight, the celebration plays once, then the badge stays interactive.\n</structure>\n\n<build>\n1. One HTML file. Export the frame's assets from Figma and place them exactly.\n2. Drive the tilt with a critically damped spring toward the cursor, so it never overshoots.\n3. Check it at 60fps and fix any frame that stutters or doesn't match the design.\n</build>\n\n<start>\nTell me which assets you exported and how the sequence runs, then build it without asking me anything else.\n</start>",
    "template": "<direction>\nBuild a badge unlock screen from {{design}}. Match the design exactly: use the file's assets, lighting, type and layout, and add only the motion.\nThe badge unlock should feel premium and celebratory: build its scene, reveal it, then celebrate with {{celebration}}.\nTreat the badge as a solid 3D object that tilts toward the cursor following real physics (mass, damping), fast and smooth, never bouncy.\nBanned: overshoot, wobble, glows the design doesn't have, anything that looks like a template.\n</direction>\n\n<structure>\nThe scene builds in, the badge arrives and settles with weight, the celebration plays once, then the badge stays interactive.\n</structure>\n\n<build>\n1. One HTML file. Export the frame's assets from Figma and place them exactly.\n2. Drive the tilt with a critically damped spring toward the cursor, so it never overshoots.\n3. Check it at 60fps and fix any frame that stutters or doesn't match the design.\n</build>\n\n<start>\nTell me which assets you exported and how the sequence runs, then build it without asking me anything else.\n</start>",
