    "summary": "Verified motion prompt by @KamStudioLabs",
    "contentBody": "Build a 45-second machine that plays an original piece of music, where every note comes from a visible collision.",
    "originalPrompt": "Build a 45-second machine that plays an original piece of music, where every note comes from a visible collision.",
    "improvedPrompt": "<direction>\nBuild a {{length}}-second machine that plays an original piece of music, where every note comes from a visible collision: {{machine}}.\nCompose the piece first, then design the machine so the physics produces it exactly: every hit lands on its note.\nStyle: {{style}}.\nBanned: notes without a visible cause, glows, generic gradients, anything that looks like a tech demo.\n</direction>\n\n<structure>\nThe machine starts quiet with one voice, adds parts as it goes, peaks, and resolves on a final hit.\n</structure>\n\n<build>\n1. Write the piece as note data (time, pitch, instrument) and synthesize it with the Web Audio API (OfflineAudioContext) to WAV.\n2. One HTML file at {{size}}. Positions are solved backwards from each note's time, so every collision is exact. Every frame is a function of time inside window.seek(t).\n3. Render with Playwright at 60fps with motion blur, then mux the audio.\n4. Watch it with sound and fix any hit that's off.\n</build>\n\n<start>\nDescribe the piece and the machine, then build it without asking me anything else. Give me the final MP4.\n</start>",
    "template": "<direction>\nBuild a {{length}}-second machine that plays an original piece of music, where every note comes from a visible collision: {{machine}}.\nCompose the piece first, then design the machine so the physics produces it exactly: every hit lands on its note.\nStyle: {{style}}.\nBanned: notes without a visible cause, glows, generic gradients, anything that looks like a tech demo.\n</direction>\n\n<structure>\nThe machine starts quiet with one voice, adds parts as it goes, peaks, and resolves on a final hit.\n</structure>\n\n<build>\n1. Write the piece as note data (time, pitch, instrument) and synthesize it with the Web Audio API (OfflineAudioContext) to WAV.\n2. One HTML file at {{size}}. Positions are solved backwards from each note's time, so every collision is exact. Every frame is a function of time inside window.seek(t).\n3. Render with Playwright at 60fps with motion blur, then mux the audio.\n4. Watch it with sound and fix any hit that's off.\n</build>\n\n<start>\nDescribe the piece and the machine, then build it without asking me anything else. Give me the final MP4.\n</start>",
